  "description": "BUSLEI crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C70 H91 Er5 O21 S4,C1 H4 O1,3(C1 H2 Cl2),H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er4 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er5 (Er) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.495-4.969 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.11-168.94°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Er5(μ4-OH)(μ3-OH)4(L1)(acac)6]·3CH2Cl2·CH3OH·H2O; empirical C74H103Cl6Er5O23S4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
